{"id": "prc:hyp-yoga-hut", "name": "The yoga-hut (yogamaṭha) and its place", "category": "body-daily-rhythm", "method_summary": "The haṭha yogin lives alone in a small hut in a well-governed, righteous land with plentiful alms and no disturbance (1.12); the hut has a small door, no holes or cracks, is neither too high nor too low, is smeared with cow-dung, clean and free of creatures, with a pavilion, raised seat and well outside and an enclosure wall (1.13); he lives there free of all worries and practises yoga by the guru's path (1.14).", "lineages": ["lin:hatha-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "1.12-1.14", "rests_on": ["tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.12", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.13", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.14"]}], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}}
{"id": "prc:hyp-diet-rules", "name": "Rules of eating in the HYP (moderate eating and foods)", "category": "body-daily-rhythm", "method_summary": "Restricted, summary only: the text gives a definition of moderate eating (mitāhāra), lists of foods it calls unwholesome and wholesome, and a first-period diet for breath practice; no lists or measures recorded.", "lineages": ["lin:hatha-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "1.58-2.14", "rests_on": ["tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.58", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.59", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.60", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.61", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.62", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:1.63", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.14"]}], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "warnings": [{"text": "atyāhāraḥ prayāsaśca prajalpo niyamagrahaḥ", "paraphrase": "the text lists overeating first among the six that destroy yoga", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "1.15"}, {"text": "prātaḥ snānopavāsādi kāyakleśavidhiṃ tathā", "paraphrase": "the text names fasting and the like as rules of bodily torment (kāyakleśa) to be avoided", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "1.61"}, {"text": "alpāhāro yadi bhavedagnirdahati tatkṣaṇāt", "paraphrase": "the text's warning in the inverted practice: if food is little, the fire burns at once", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "3.81"}], "restricted": true}
{"id": "prc:hyp-pranayama-summary", "name": "Breath-control (prāṇāyāma) in the HYP", "category": "breath", "method_summary": "Restricted, summary only: the text teaches breath-control after firm posture under the guru's path, with a channel-purifying practice, eight named retentions and the two kinds of retention (sahita, kevala); no method, counts or times recorded.", "lineages": ["lin:hatha-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.1-2.73", "rests_on": ["tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.1", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.6", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.44", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.71", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.72", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.73"]}], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "warnings": [{"text": "śanaireva na vegataḥ", "paraphrase": "breath is to be let out only slowly, not with force", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.9"}, {"text": "anyathā hanti sādhakam", "paraphrase": "otherwise it kills the practitioner", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.15"}, {"text": "ayuktābhyāsayogena sarvarogasamudbhavaḥ", "paraphrase": "from improper practice all disease arises", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.16"}, {"text": "bhavanti vividhā rogāḥ pavanasya prakopataḥ", "paraphrase": "various diseases arise from the disturbance of the breath", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.17"}, {"text": "gurūpadiṣṭamārgeṇa", "paraphrase": "by the path taught by the guru", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.1"}, {"text": "śanaiḥ śanaireva recayennaiva vegataḥ", "paraphrase": "again: only slowly, never with force", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "3.13"}], "restricted": true}
{"id": "prc:hyp-nadi-shodhana-summary", "name": "Purification of the channels by breath (HYP 2.7-10)", "category": "breath", "method_summary": "Restricted, summary only: a breath practice through the two sides said to purify the groups of channels; no method, counts or times recorded.", "lineages": ["lin:hatha-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.5-2.10", "rests_on": ["tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.5", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.6", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.7", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.8", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.9", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.10"]}], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "warnings": [{"text": "śanaireva na vegataḥ", "paraphrase": "slowly, not with force", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.9"}], "restricted": true}
{"id": "prc:hyp-satkarma-summary", "name": "The six cleansing acts (ṣaṭkarma) in the HYP", "category": "cleansing", "method_summary": "Restricted, summary only: the text names six acts, dhauti, basti, neti, trāṭaka, nauli and kapālabhāti (2.22), and gajakaraṇī (2.38), for a person with excess fat or phlegm only (2.21); no method recorded.", "lineages": ["lin:hatha-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.21-2.38", "rests_on": ["tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.21", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.22", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.23", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.36", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.37", "tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:2.38"]}], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "warnings": [{"text": "anyastu nācarettāni doṣāṇāṃ samabhāvataḥ", "paraphrase": "another (whose humours are in balance) should not do them", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.21"}, {"text": "ācāryāṇāntu keṣāñcidanyat karma na sammatam", "paraphrase": "some ācāryas do not approve of any other act than breath-control", "source": "src:hatha-yoga-pradipika", "ref": "2.37"}], "restricted": true}
